  "details": "Currently the camera allows publishing a spout stream, which is very useful for a multitude of things. There is still a inherint limitation however in that the camera does not allow you to specify the layer masks directly. This means there is no current way to disable post processing on a vrchat camera, which is devastating when trying to capture raw data streams out of the game. One solution to this would be to add a post processing toggle to the camera, but another solution would be to allow worlds to use a component to specify additional spout streams. This would allow a world to have mutliple different active outputs, all with different layers or even coming directly from render textures",
